From d2cdd37058ef20489be256d821987da0688e044f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wendell Britt <wendell@masteringallyship.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 22:17:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Send the superpower quiz result it already promised

captureSuperpowerLead returned "Saved. Your result is on its way to your
inbox." and had no send path at all -- it imported db, syncSubscriber
and the list contract, and nothing else. The address was stored and
tagged and the person received nothing.

The reveal states its terms before it asks for the address ("I will send
your result and the Face you ranked last"), which made this the one
capture surface on the site that discloses the deal up front and the one
that was breaking it.

Adds SuperpowerResultEmail, scoped to exactly what the page promised --
the home Face, the Face ranked last, and Chapter 9's reason the second
is worth more. Nothing is sold in it; an email that arrives carrying a
pitch instead of the result is the same broken promise in a nicer suit.
Styling mirrors ChapterOneEmail so both sends read as one sender.

Wires it into the action on the established persist-then-send shape, and
varies the returned message on the send result the way
captureChapterOneLead already does, so an unconfigured or failing
provider no longer reports success it did not achieve.

tsc --noEmit and eslint both clean.
